      "dom_id": "question-52367",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\frac{2x-6}{3-x}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any factors that they have in common.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x-6}{3-x} & =\\frac{2(x-3)}{-(x-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot (x-3)}{(-1)\\cdot (x-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot \\cancel{(x-3)}}{(-1)\\cdot \\cancel{(x-3)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(-1)} \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
